 "notes": "Rules implemented faithfully (day-2 fade toward the week's first RTH open; stop max(1x dist, 0.15%); target WO; time exit 11:30; one trade/week). Published default max_dist=0.25 yields only 10 (MNQ) / 21 (MES) / 10 (MGC) trades in 21 months and is flat-to-negative on MNQ (PF 0.93) and negative on all three in 2023-24. At max_dist=0.50 MES is the MAIN standout (35 trades, PF 2.09, Sharpe 1.41, 76% positive months) but collapses on PRIOR (54 trades, PF 0.67), so it is not robust; MNQ at max_dist=0.50 is the only cell positive in both periods (MAIN 21 trades PF 1.27; PRIOR 43 trades PF 1.59) but with Sharpe 0.34 and a 4% Lucid pass rate. require_eth_touch hurts everywhere (opposite of the study); allow_day3 adds losers on MAIN; min_stop_pct 0.30 changes little. Frequency (<= 2 trades/month) is too low for a standalone eval; at best a small portfolio leg. Lucid expected net per eval is negative for every cell on every instrument. Alternative MNQ final: results/mr_wkopen/best_MNQ_main_*.csv.",
